Subject: [PATCH] build: point ETHERLAB/RUCKIG/ECMCCFG at the site package tree

SITE-SPECIFIC.  Skip this patch unless your site lays modules out the way PCDS
does.  It is carried here because without it the build cannot find its
dependencies, and an undocumented local edit is worse than a reviewed patch.

ecmc's `configure/RELEASE` defaults every external module to `$(SUPPORT)/...`,
a sibling of `epics-base`.  PCDS installs them under `$PSPKG_ROOT` in versioned
directories, which no default matches:

    ETHERLAB = $(SUPPORT)/etherlab          ->  <ecmc>/../etherlab
    actual                                  ->  $PSPKG_ROOT/etherlab -> /opt/etherlab

The `?= /opt/etherlab` fallback in `devEcmcSup/Makefile` does not rescue this.
`?=` assigns only when a variable is unset, and `RELEASE` is read first, so the
fallback never fires.  The build looks in the source checkout, where the built
library lives in `lib/.libs/` rather than `lib/`, and fails as if the library
were missing.

Setting these in `CONFIG_SITE` rather than `RELEASE` is deliberate: `RELEASE`
is subject to `CHECK_RELEASE = YES` consistency checking against every other
module's `RELEASE`, and these paths are local to this build.

`$(PSPKG_ROOT)` is an environment variable, so the paths are parameterised
rather than hardcoded -- but the version directories (`R0.19.4`, `R11.0.8`,
`R0.2.16`) are not, and will need updating on any version bump.  They are
recorded in `sites/pcds.conf` too; keep the two in step.

The example IOC is a separate EPICS application with its own `configure/`, and
inherits nothing from the module's.  It needs the same settings or it fails the
same way -- which is exactly how this was found.

### The alternative, if you would rather not patch

Both files end with:

    -include $(TOP)/configure/CONFIG_SITE.local

so the same five lines in an untracked `configure/CONFIG_SITE.local` work
without touching a tracked file.  That is arguably the more correct home for
site paths.  This patch exists because a tracked, reviewed change is easier to
audit six months later than a file that only exists on one machine.  Choose one
-- doing both means two places to update.

Applies to: ecmc v11.0.8
Verified on: SLAC PCDS, EPICS base R7.0.3.1-2.0, rhel9-x86_64
---
 configure/CONFIG_SITE                | 5 +++++
 ecmcExampleTop/configure/CONFIG_SITE | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/configure/CONFIG_SITE b/configure/CONFIG_SITE
--- a/configure/CONFIG_SITE
+++ b/configure/CONFIG_SITE
@@ -37,6 +37,11 @@

 USR_CXXFLAGS += -DUSE_TYPED_RSET

+EXPRTK = $(TOP)/exprtkSupport
+RUCKIG = $(PSPKG_ROOT)/ruckig/R0.19.4
+ETHERLAB = $(PSPKG_ROOT)/etherlab
+ECMCCFG = $(PSPKG_ROOT)/ecmccfg/R11.0.8
+ECMCCOMP = $(PSPKG_ROOT)/ecmccomp/R0.2.16

 # These allow developers to override the CONFIG_SITE variable
 # settings without having to modify the configure/CONFIG_SITE
diff --git a/ecmcExampleTop/configure/CONFIG_SITE b/ecmcExampleTop/configure/CONFIG_SITE
--- a/ecmcExampleTop/configure/CONFIG_SITE
+++ b/ecmcExampleTop/configure/CONFIG_SITE
@@ -35,6 +35,12 @@
 #HOST_OPT = NO
 #CROSS_OPT = NO

+EXPRTK = $(TOP)/exprtkSupport
+RUCKIG = $(PSPKG_ROOT)/ruckig/R0.19.4
+ETHERLAB = $(PSPKG_ROOT)/etherlab
+ECMCCFG = $(PSPKG_ROOT)/ecmccfg/R11.0.8
+ECMCCOMP = $(PSPKG_ROOT)/ecmccomp/R0.2.16
+
 # These allow developers to override the CONFIG_SITE variable
 # settings without having to modify the configure/CONFIG_SITE
 # file itself.
